# AGENTS.md

Rules for every AI agent working in this repository. `CLAUDE.md` imports this file; Cursor, Codex, and OpenCode read it natively. Keep it to what an agent cannot find by looking and needs on every quest: a file listing, or a command a manifest already shows, goes stale here.

{{OVERVIEW}}

{{QUALITY_BAR}}

## Reading protocol

An agent assigned a quest reads exactly this file, its one quest file in `.quests/`, and the files that quest names in `touched_files` or its body points to. It does not scan `.quests/` or read other quest files, `ROADMAP.md`, or `CHANGELOG.md` unless its quest cites them. When a `depends_on` quest is not yet in `.quests/done/`, it stops and reports the blocker.

## Acceptance

    {{ACCEPTANCE}}

A change is acceptable when this passes. A quest file's acceptance criteria name the exact command for that quest.

## Work tracking

Strategy lives in [`ROADMAP.md`](ROADMAP.md), atomic work in [`.quests/`](.quests/) (one file per quest, its `parent` naming the roadmap Quest chain it serves, or the Campaign for a Side quest, one in no chain), and finished work in [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md).

A change finished in one sitting, with nothing anyone must agree first, needs no quest file: make it and run the acceptance command. Work that spans sittings or goes to another agent gets a quest file. Behaviour a person must agree before it is built gets a written spec first.

Lifecycle `open -> in_progress -> done`. On completion:

1. Confirm the acceptance command passes and every `depends_on` quest is in `.quests/done/`.
2. Move the file to `.quests/done/` with `status: done`, and add one `../` to each of its relative links.
3. Add one dated line to [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) naming the quest id, and strike a finished Quest chain through in `ROADMAP.md`.

